@startuml
!include ../../common/eztrade-style.puml

title EZTrade Backend - Domain Event Flow

component "TradingService" as Trading EZ_BACKEND
component "trading SpringDomainEventPublisher" as TradingPublisher
component "Wallet TradingEventsListener" as WalletListener EZ_FRONTEND
component "WalletService" as Wallet EZ_BACKEND
component "wallet SpringDomainEventPublisher" as WalletPublisher
component "Portfolio TradingEventsListener" as PortfolioTradingListener EZ_FRONTEND
component "Portfolio WalletEventsListener" as PortfolioWalletListener EZ_FRONTEND
component "PortfolioService" as Portfolio EZ_BACKEND
component "portfolio SpringDomainEventPublisher" as PortfolioPublisher
component "Notifications DomainEventsListener\n@TransactionalEventListener(AFTER_COMMIT)\n@Async" as NotificationsListener EZ_FRONTEND
component "NotificationService" as Notifications EZ_BACKEND

Trading --> TradingPublisher : OrderPlacedEvent\nOrderCancelledEvent\nOrderExecutionRequestEvent
TradingPublisher ..> WalletListener : Spring Event
WalletListener --> Wallet : handle(...)

Wallet --> WalletPublisher : FundsReservedEvent\nFundsReleasedEvent\nFundsSettledEvent\nInsufficientFundsEvent\nAvailableCashUpdatedEvent\nOrderExecutedEvent
WalletPublisher ..> PortfolioTradingListener : OrderExecutedEvent
WalletPublisher ..> PortfolioWalletListener : AvailableCashUpdatedEvent
PortfolioTradingListener --> Portfolio : update positions
PortfolioWalletListener --> Portfolio : update cash projection

Portfolio --> PortfolioPublisher : PortfolioValuationUpdatedEvent\nPositionOpened/Closed/Changed
TradingPublisher ..> NotificationsListener : order events
WalletPublisher ..> NotificationsListener : InsufficientFundsEvent
PortfolioPublisher ..> NotificationsListener : PortfolioValuationUpdatedEvent
NotificationsListener --> Notifications : builds and sends message

note right of WalletListener
OrderPlacedEvent is handled synchronously in wallet:
if BUY funds cannot be reserved, trading aborts.
end note

note bottom of NotificationsListener
Notifications are handled after commit with fallbackExecution=true
and @Async. This evidence comes from DomainEventsListener.java.
end note

@enduml
